# Core desktop — everything needed for a usable Hyprland session.
# One package per line. '#' comments and blank lines ignored.
# Prefix a line with 'aur:' to route it through the AUR helper.

## Compositor + Hypr ecosystem
hyprland
hyprpaper
hyprlock
hypridle
hyprpicker
hyprshot
hyprpolkitagent
hyprcursor
hyprlauncher
hyprland-qt-support
hyprtoolkit

## Portals — screen sharing, file pickers.
# The hyprland portal must be present; xdg-desktop-portal-wlr is deliberately
# NOT here, it competes for the ScreenCast interface and breaks capture.
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk

## Session plumbing
polkit
gnome-keyring
qt5-wayland
qt6-wayland

## Launchers
# hyprlauncher is the native one (SUPER+H); rofi and wofi are kept as the
# themed launchers on SUPER+R / SUPER+W. rofi also backs the cliphist picker.
rofi
wofi

## Bar, terminal, notifications, clipboard
waybar
kitty
dunst
cliphist
wl-clipboard

## Audio
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
pavucontrol
playerctl

## File manager + viewers (KDE apps, no full Plasma session)
dolphin
gwenview
okular
ark
ffmpegthumbnailer
kdegraphics-thumbnailers
kimageformats
qt6-imageformats

## Fonts + icons
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-dejavu
ttf-liberation
ttf-font-awesome
ttf-firacode-nerd
papirus-icon-theme
# waybar's wlr/taskbar uses the Numix-Circle theme. It is NOT in
# numix-icon-theme-git (that ships Numix and Numix-Light only) — it needs this
# separate package, or the taskbar silently falls back to default icons.
aur:numix-circle-icon-theme-git

## Theming bridge (Qt apps follow the dark theme)
kvantum
qt6ct

## Basics
git
base-devel
curl
zsh
jq
tree
brightnessctl
network-manager-applet
